      "body": [
        {
          "callee": "local/low_level",
          "id": "GfBWA62jJlLFVdNKS0OUh",
          "parameters": [
            {
              "expression": "\"PUBLISH\"",
              "name": "command",
              "type": "tel"
            },
            {
              "expression": "[channel, message]",
              "name": "args",
              "type": "tel"
            }
          ],
          "storeAs": "output",
          "type": "call"
        },
        {
          "id": "sO8eQOerydvwLS_HPAOvD",
          "type": "return",
          "value": "output"
        }
      ],
      "description": "Posts a message to the given channel.\n\nIn a Redis Cluster clients can publish to every node. The cluster makes sure that published messages are forwarded as needed, so clients can subscribe to any channel by connecting to any one of the nodes.\n\n**Available since:**\n2.0.0    \n**Time complexity:**\nO(N+M) where N is the number of clients subscribed to the receiving channel and M is the total number of subscribed patterns (by any client).   \n**ACL categories:**\n@pubsub, @fast",
      "exported": true,
      "id": "wznWlqx40gQlL2iFM9QGl",
      "name": "PUBLISH",
      "parameters": [
        {
          "description": "Name of the Redis PubSub channel",
          "name": "channel",
          "optional": false,
          "type": "tel",
          "valueDescription": "string"
        },
        {
          "description": "Message to send",
          "name": "message",
          "optional": false,
          "type": "tel",
          "valueDescription": "string | number | boolean"
        }
      ],
      "type": "defineFunction"
    }
